# clangd configuration for sonotron.
#
# Point clangd at the host build's compilation database. build/host is the
# canonical full host build (CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS=ON), regenerated on
# every `cmake -S . -B build/host`, so it stays current as new files are added.
#
# Why this matters: the root compile_commands.json symlink historically pointed
# at build/tidy, which goes stale — files added after its last configure are
# absent from the DB, so clangd cannot see how to compile them and falls back to
# guessing, producing phantom diagnostics ("'test.hpp' file not found",
# "'CHECK' undeclared", "std::string aka int"). Pointing at the regularly-
# reconfigured build/host DB fixes that class of false positive.
#
# The dual-target arm-none-eabi DB (build/arm) is deliberately NOT used: those
# freestanding compile commands drop std::string/exceptions, and if clangd used
# them for a shared header it would report host-side std:: types as unavailable.
# Host flags keep std:: resolving correctly.
#
# Residual (not fixable by config alone): files inside .claude/worktrees/ during
# a multi-agent run are absent from this DB (transient — they resolve once the
# worktrees are cleaned), and a header genuinely compiled for BOTH host and arm
# can only carry one config, so occasional core-header noise remains. Always
# treat clangd here as advisory; the ground truth is `cmake --build` + `ctest`.
CompileFlags:
  CompilationDatabase: build/host
